@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Contact API
	Testing Koroneiki Contact API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the external links for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| 1234 |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: Create and view contact
	Koroneiki contacts created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | false                                    |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | false                                    |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |

Scenario: Create and view contact with verified email address
	Koroneiki verified contacts created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |

Scenario: Create and view contact via uuid
	Koroneiki contacts created via API should be viewable via API using the uuid value.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via uuid and the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |

Scenario: Update contact and view
	Koroneiki contacts updated via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name              | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name              | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Update contact via uuid and view
	Koroneiki contacts updated via API using uuid should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via uuid to have the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name              | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Delete contact and view
	Koroneiki contacts deleted via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I delete a contact on koroneiki with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

