	Koroneiki verified contacts deleted via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And I delete a contact on koroneiki with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Delete contact via uuid and view
	Koroneiki contacts deleted via API using the uuid should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I delete a contact on koroneiki with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via uuid
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Create and view contact external link
	Koroneiki contact external links created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And I create a nested field for the contact external link with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address              | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| External Link Nested Field | ${staticContactExternalLinksNestedField} |
	| First Name                 | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language                   | English                                  |
	| Last Name                  | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name                | User                                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |

Scenario: Create and view contact external link with mapped URL
	Koroneiki contact external links with mapped URLs created via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | Koroneiki |
	| Entity Id   | 1234      |
	| Entity Name | Generic   |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | Koroneiki                          |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                               |
	| Entity Name | Generic                            |
	| URL         | https://koroneiki.liferay.com/1234 |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | Koroneiki                          |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                               |
	| Entity Name | Generic                            |
	| URL         | https://koroneiki.liferay.com/1234 |

Scenario: Remove contact external link and view
	Koroneiki contact external links removed via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And I delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: View contact audit entries
	Koroneiki contact changes via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin" via the audit entry key
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki Admin" via the audit entry key

Scenario: View contact audit entries by agent
	Koroneiki contact changes via API via an agent should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Agent Name    | Koroneiki User                           |
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Agent Name    | Koroneiki User                           |
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "" to the new value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User" via the audit entry key
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" field "Email Address" from the old value "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the new value "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" executed by "Koroneiki User" via the audit entry key

Scenario: View contact audit entries by admin and agent
	Koroneiki contact changes via API via an agent and admin should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
